{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.72,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D18", "D20", "D32"],
      "pins": ["D18.2", "D20.2", "D32.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0110"],
      "observed": "The anodes of D18, D20, and D32 are tied together on /NET0110, but /NET0110 has no other nodes and is not connected to +3V3 or any other supply.",
      "expected": "Status LEDs driven by CM4 active-low Ethernet/activity outputs should have their anodes connected to a supply rail (normally +3V3), as other LEDs on the board are.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"23\") (name \"/NET0110\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D18\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D20\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D32\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") (class \"Med Power\") ... (node (ref \"D37\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) ...)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The Ethernet link LEDs and Pi activity LED will not light because their common anode node is floating; intended visual status indication is lost.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U30", "U35"],
      "pins": ["U30.4", "U30.5", "U35.4", "U35.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "Both the isolated-side ground pin (GND2, pin 5) and the logic-side ground pin (GND1, pin 4) of the isolated CAN transceivers U30 and U35 are connected to the same GND net.",
      "expected": "For an isolated CAN transceiver/bus, GND2 should be a separate isolated ground domain, not tied to GND1/GND; the specification states the board implements isolated CAN buses through isolated CAN transceivers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U30\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"U30\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (`U8`, `U9`) through an isolated CAN transceiver (`U11`/companion)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The CAN buses are not galvanically isolated as intended, removing the isolation barrier and increasing susceptibility to ground loops/noise between the rover compute board and motor/actuator CAN devices.",
      "confidence": 0.65
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R22"],
      "pins": ["R22.1", "R22.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R22 is given the schematic value 24k, but its description and MPN identify a 24Ω resistor.",
      "expected": "A resistor across the VOUTP/VOUTN clamp/bleeder network should have a consistent high-impedance value; the 24k value is consistent with the surrounding 51k/249k divider and the SPICE deck, while 24Ω would be a heavy load.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R22\") (value \"24k\") ... (description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") (value \"FRC0805J240TSD\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R22 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If assembled from the MPN/description rather than the schematic value, R22 would load VOUTP/VOUTN by 1000x, potentially overheating, altering the clamp/protection behavior, and possibly damaging the associated bridge/rectifier path.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain at least one clear connectivity anomaly: D18/D20/D32 LED anodes are left floating on /NET0110, so those status LEDs cannot operate. Supporting evidence also shows isolated CAN transceiver grounds tied together and a resistor value/MPN mismatch on R22."
}

